From 35f1ee105f583da05c97ffbc2c2c17075d2c67d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:52:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban capability owner: skip the requester's bound
 origin placeholder in create_overlap; wake on a rejected owner request

Hub card t_01a1d49003c65ca4 (placed on the hub by macbook; macbook placeholder t_01a1d48f676074bc, scheduled,
same title) blocked with needs=['host:macbook']. macbook refused the owner create as create_overlap whose only
match was that placeholder, no owner existed, and wait-check exited 2 until the card was woken
wake_check_broken 4 minutes later with nothing done (t_01a1d4dc5eb85b00).

Five whys:
1. No owner card: macbook's kanban_create refused create_overlap (sent row, matches=[t_01a1d48f676074bc]).
2. The placeholder matched: the owner title/body quote the waiting card's title, which the placeholder shares.
3. It was not exempt: overlap_exclusions only walked the waiting card and its awaiting.ref chain upward; the
   placeholder waits on the hub card (downward), and the holder-side scan only skipped card["id"] == waiting.
4. Nothing modelled "a card bound to the waiting card" on either side.
5. A rejected request was mapped to wait-check exit 2 ("cannot tell"), so the dispatcher treated a terminal
   refusal as a broken probe instead of waking the card with it.

Fix:
- Requester: kanban_capability_routing.bound_cards() adds the origin placeholder named in the forward footer
  ("This card was <gw> card <id>; it completes there ...") and local cards parked on the waiting card to
  overlap_exclusions, so they ride distinct_from.
- Holder: kanban_overlap skips, for a capability-owner create, a local card forwarded to the waiting card
  (placement_forwarded.remote_task_id) or scheduled with awaiting.ref == the waiting card. Older requesters
  that send no distinct_from for it are covered too. Same-title strangers still refuse.
- wait_check: a request in a failed terminal state exits 0 at once with the refusal text (code, matches,
  error) so the card wakes to re-plan; owner_status keeps refusing a park on a dead request.

Tests: test_kanban_capability_owner_origin_mirror.py (RED on main: 6/6 fail; GREEN here), and
test_kanban_capability_routing.py's two rejected-request tests now pin the wake-with-refusal contract (RED on
main: 2 fail).
